WEBVTT

00:00:05.079 --> 00:00:09.079
www.titlovi.com

00:00:12.079 --> 00:00:17.039
When are we born?
When do we die?

00:00:17.685 --> 00:00:21.485
Why are we born?
Why do we die?

00:00:21.989 --> 00:00:26.619
This world has been destroyed
and reborn time and again,

00:00:27.061 --> 00:00:30.622
being resurrected each time
as Paradise.

00:00:31.432 --> 00:00:34.959
It has happened before,
and will happen again.

00:00:36.303 --> 00:00:38.271
The endless cycle
of life and death.

00:00:38.372 --> 00:00:41.967
This world is a Paradise
which someone opened.

00:00:43.411 --> 00:00:47.973
This era is almost
at an end.

00:00:49.583 --> 00:00:55.647
We have acquired the means to live
longer than our natural spans,

00:00:56.924 --> 00:01:00.826
but little did we suspect
that this world has an end.

00:01:01.529 --> 00:01:04.498
I have despaired
at the ending world.

00:01:05.399 --> 00:01:10.063
My fate has fallen and scattered
like the flower petals.

00:01:10.638 --> 00:01:14.597
And as if by
a sandstorm,

00:01:15.209 --> 00:01:18.201
it simply wears down
and weathers away.

00:01:18.879 --> 00:01:24.476
As if to be purified, the world
will be encased in ice...

00:01:24.919 --> 00:01:27.217
...so that it may be returned
to the beginning.

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:37.859
Paradise is a world
which someone opens.

00:02:29.617 --> 00:02:32.119
This was the place,
all right...

00:02:32.119 --> 00:02:32.949
Hige...

00:02:34.255 --> 00:02:37.918
I gave her my word.
I promised Blue.

00:02:38.859 --> 00:02:44.456
I said that I'd make it back no matter what,
so she should wait for me here.

00:02:44.965 --> 00:02:46.700
The situation's changed.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:50.830
With all that's happened, I bet even Blue
had no choice but to make a run for it.

00:02:51.272 --> 00:02:54.264
Or maybe she didn't believe
what you said?

00:02:57.044 --> 00:02:59.103
Hige made things right!

00:02:59.513 --> 00:03:00.946
Let's just drop it...

00:03:01.582 --> 00:03:02.549
Kiba...

00:03:15.462 --> 00:03:17.896
You must all
go to Paradise.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:22.169
The <i>true</i> Paradise
meant for all of you.

00:03:23.571 --> 00:03:24.663
Cheza...

00:03:25.139 --> 00:03:27.039
I'm... okay.

00:03:27.641 --> 00:03:29.836
I'm feeling
a lot better...

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:31.372
You must go there.

00:03:38.185 --> 00:03:40.380
Kiba! That's enough,
make her stop!

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:47.827
Take her.

00:03:53.434 --> 00:03:54.628
Grab on.

00:03:56.537 --> 00:03:59.005
Aren't you going
to say anything?

00:03:59.974 --> 00:04:01.532
Like how
Jaguara and I...

00:04:04.945 --> 00:04:06.435
You told me
this once.

00:04:08.382 --> 00:04:11.146
Pride doesn't count for much
if you're dead.

00:04:12.386 --> 00:04:15.787
We've been trying to reach
Paradise from the very beginning.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:17.484
Together.

00:04:17.825 --> 00:04:20.055
That hasn't changed,
not even now.

00:04:21.228 --> 00:04:22.855
That's all that matters.

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:52.524
How long are you gonna
keep following me?

00:04:53.861 --> 00:04:56.989
There's no need for you
to stay with me.

00:04:57.965 --> 00:05:00.195
Let's go back to where
I found you.

00:05:00.501 --> 00:05:01.900
The guys are waiting.

00:05:02.369 --> 00:05:05.361
If we went back,
I know we could find them.

00:05:07.374 --> 00:05:08.602
I'm okay...

00:05:09.877 --> 00:05:12.107
I'm hungry,
that's all.

00:05:13.047 --> 00:05:19.543
Have you... Have you hated me
all this time?

00:05:21.455 --> 00:05:23.719
Hated you?
Why?

00:05:24.224 --> 00:05:27.494
You're telling me that you've
forgiven me for hating wolves...

00:05:27.494 --> 00:05:30.930
...and trying to kill
every last one of them?

00:05:32.132 --> 00:05:33.690
As if that would
ever happen.

00:05:40.708 --> 00:05:45.611
I never knew that I had
some wolf in me.

00:05:46.847 --> 00:05:53.150
It was only after I met Cheza and the guys...
the wolves... that I finally realized it.

00:05:55.456 --> 00:05:58.220
If I had known that
I can talk like this...

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:02.261
I only wish I could've
done this sooner.

00:06:16.276 --> 00:06:17.607
Wait! Stop!

00:06:31.959 --> 00:06:32.983
Pops!

00:06:34.361 --> 00:06:35.828
Pops!

00:06:37.765 --> 00:06:38.732
What is it?

00:06:40.567 --> 00:06:43.434
Forget it.
It's nothing.

00:06:51.278 --> 00:06:52.939
I've got a bad feeling
about this.

00:07:00.421 --> 00:07:04.380
I can't believe I've gotten the chance to walk
with my arm around your shoulder again.

00:07:04.825 --> 00:07:07.487
How can you be
so nonchalant?

00:07:08.695 --> 00:07:12.461
It's best to think of pleasant
things at times like these.

00:07:13.367 --> 00:07:14.891
How forward-looking
of you.

00:07:15.636 --> 00:07:17.968
Because there's nothing
to see behind us.

00:07:21.475 --> 00:07:22.576
A car?

00:07:22.576 --> 00:07:23.838
I'll go take a look.

00:07:24.478 --> 00:07:25.240
Hubb?

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:27.539
Hey!

00:07:27.948 --> 00:07:28.937
Hey!

00:07:30.384 --> 00:07:32.614
Hello?!
Is anybody there?!

00:07:45.432 --> 00:07:47.400
They had a
falling out, huh?

00:07:47.935 --> 00:07:49.368
Go and check
the back.

00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:07.881
They sure were relaxed
about all this.

00:08:08.322 --> 00:08:10.256
What were they planning
to celebrate, anyway?

00:08:10.924 --> 00:08:14.155
No luck at all.
There's nothing useful back there.

00:08:14.695 --> 00:08:16.629
There isn't all that
much fuel, either.

00:08:17.331 --> 00:08:21.097
Still, we can move
forward for now.

00:08:26.507 --> 00:08:27.565
Cher...

00:08:29.409 --> 00:08:33.470
Where should
the two of us go?

00:08:42.923 --> 00:08:45.448
I smell Blue,
all right...

00:08:50.163 --> 00:08:51.095
Hige!

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:59.906
What a stink...
This is human blood.

00:09:01.208 --> 00:09:04.234
This is Blue's
old man!

00:09:04.811 --> 00:09:07.109
Maybe Blue
is with him.

00:09:08.849 --> 00:09:11.340
If she's gone back
to her old master,

00:09:11.618 --> 00:09:14.018
maybe she's better off
this way.

00:09:14.421 --> 00:09:16.023
That's not for you
to decide!

00:09:16.023 --> 00:09:18.218
She's just a
half-assed wolf.

00:09:19.893 --> 00:09:23.158
Do you seriously think she can get
to Paradise with the rest of us?

00:09:23.497 --> 00:09:24.429
Drop it.

00:09:24.765 --> 00:09:27.859
Do we have time to spare
to keep making these detours?

00:09:34.908 --> 00:09:36.034
Hige...

00:09:51.858 --> 00:09:53.553
Son of a bitch...

00:09:54.061 --> 00:09:57.861
With all this blowing snow, I can't see
my hand in front of my face...

00:09:58.699 --> 00:10:01.497
It's stopped snowing,
Pops.

00:10:02.970 --> 00:10:07.998
Have you always
called me that...?

00:10:09.242 --> 00:10:13.941
It ain't like I'm your parent
or anything like that...

00:10:15.582 --> 00:10:16.879
I know that.

00:10:17.884 --> 00:10:21.820
But you're like a father to me,
so what else can I do?

00:10:23.624 --> 00:10:27.458
I wanted to stay with you
for my whole life.

00:10:28.595 --> 00:10:35.467
It ain't like I believed
what you told me...

00:10:36.303 --> 00:10:40.797
I ain't like I trust
wolves now...

00:10:43.143 --> 00:10:45.703
But I know this
for sure.

00:10:46.647 --> 00:10:50.344
I know that wolves would never
do something that cruel.

00:10:50.884 --> 00:10:51.851
For one thing...

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:54.144
Pops?

00:10:58.425 --> 00:10:59.323
Pops!

00:11:00.227 --> 00:11:02.559
Snap out of it!
Pops!

00:11:08.735 --> 00:11:09.702
Don't fall asleep!

00:11:11.505 --> 00:11:13.405
Hang in there!
Stay awake!

00:11:19.546 --> 00:11:23.107
If we keep moving on, I'm sure
we'll run into the others...

00:11:24.084 --> 00:11:27.520
If we run into them,
I know we'll...

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:58.777
Mr. Yaiden?
Can you see me?

00:11:59.186 --> 00:12:00.414
Mr. Yaiden!

00:12:02.622 --> 00:12:04.556
His eyes seem
to be working.

00:12:04.891 --> 00:12:08.691
He doesn't seem to have any major fractures,
but I'm not sure about his brain.

00:12:09.262 --> 00:12:11.025
Is Pops gonna die?

00:12:11.364 --> 00:12:15.698
It's all right. It'll take a little time
for him to regain his strength, though.

00:12:16.336 --> 00:12:17.564
Oh...

00:12:23.477 --> 00:12:25.001
I saw Paradise.

00:12:27.214 --> 00:12:28.374
I saw it.

00:12:28.982 --> 00:12:31.041
I saw the Paradise that the
Nobles tried to open up.

00:12:31.618 --> 00:12:33.449
The Nobles' Paradise?

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:37.356
Yeah.
A false Paradise.

00:12:38.125 --> 00:12:43.495
Now I know. Paradise is something
that wolves have to open.

00:12:44.498 --> 00:12:47.729
There is only one place
that can be called Paradise.

00:12:48.668 --> 00:12:50.863
There should
only <i>be</i> one.

00:12:55.976 --> 00:12:58.809
This cigar was meant to celebrate
the opening of Paradise, huh?

00:13:00.313 --> 00:13:03.111
Can we go to
their Paradise, too?

00:13:03.817 --> 00:13:05.978
No.
I doubt it.

00:13:06.253 --> 00:13:08.118
What are we supposed
to <i>do,</i> then?

00:13:08.655 --> 00:13:11.556
All we can do
is die out.

00:13:12.759 --> 00:13:14.021
Why?!

00:13:14.461 --> 00:13:16.929
Because it would become
a distorted world.

00:13:18.231 --> 00:13:24.932
But in a new world created by wolves, I'm certain
that new humans will be created, too.

00:13:25.872 --> 00:13:28.670
So we're just pawns
to be thrown away, huh?

00:13:29.876 --> 00:13:31.104
Suits me fine.

00:13:33.446 --> 00:13:38.315
I think I understand now why
we could never have children.

00:13:40.086 --> 00:13:43.647
On some level, we had sensed
that the world was ending.

00:13:44.491 --> 00:13:46.721
It seemed like we had found
something else to obsess over,

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:49.051
but the fact is that we had
given up on the future.

00:13:49.796 --> 00:13:53.425
That's the reason why we
could never get pregnant.

00:13:54.134 --> 00:13:56.034
Do you still
feel that way?

00:13:56.503 --> 00:13:59.802
What sort of hope am I supposed
to have in a situation like this?

00:14:00.473 --> 00:14:03.567
Right now,
I'm here with you.

00:14:04.077 --> 00:14:07.012
Something that I had given up on
has come true.

00:14:07.447 --> 00:14:09.039
No matter what happens
to the world,

00:14:09.482 --> 00:14:12.110
right now, I want to have
faith in the future.

00:14:14.221 --> 00:14:15.620
You've changed,
you know that?

00:14:17.791 --> 00:14:18.655
Stop!

00:14:18.992 --> 00:14:20.050
Stop the car!

00:14:29.269 --> 00:14:30.634
Hige!
Hang in there!

00:14:38.378 --> 00:14:39.367
Hige!

00:14:42.749 --> 00:14:43.716
Hige!

00:14:44.317 --> 00:14:45.284
Hige!

00:14:56.796 --> 00:14:57.956
Cheza!

00:15:08.775 --> 00:15:12.836
It certainly seems like this world
is really heading towards destruction.

00:15:13.914 --> 00:15:16.212
Is escaping to some other world
the only way out?

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:21.013
If we could fly through the sky and reach
some other world somewhere...

00:15:21.588 --> 00:15:22.748
Why?

00:15:23.890 --> 00:15:26.324
Why do humans do nothing
but look at the sky?

00:15:27.227 --> 00:15:30.253
Why do you want to fly even though
you don't have wings?

00:15:31.765 --> 00:15:33.164
As for us,
we run.

00:15:35.068 --> 00:15:38.697
We keep running on our own legs
no matter how far we have to go.

00:15:44.878 --> 00:15:47.108
Where is Kiba?
And the others?

00:15:47.714 --> 00:15:50.376
It's all right.
They're following us.

00:15:55.088 --> 00:15:56.248
Say, Hubb?

00:15:57.090 --> 00:15:58.491
Have you noticed?

00:15:58.491 --> 00:15:59.459
Noticed what?

00:15:59.459 --> 00:16:01.620
You've stopped sneezing.

00:16:03.196 --> 00:16:04.424
Hey, you're right!

00:16:04.798 --> 00:16:06.663
Were my allergies overloaded
or something?

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:10.367
Maybe I built up a tolerance by
being around wolves all this time.

00:16:10.837 --> 00:16:12.566
I don't think immunities
work that way.

00:16:14.374 --> 00:16:16.035
Maybe you did.

00:16:16.676 --> 00:16:20.373
I'm surrounded by all sorts of things
that I didn't think were possible.

00:16:20.814 --> 00:16:23.248
Yeah.
That's for sure.

00:16:23.917 --> 00:16:25.885
And the most impossible
thing of all...

00:16:28.922 --> 00:16:32.585
...is that you came
to look for me.

00:16:50.477 --> 00:16:51.444
What the...?

00:17:32.519 --> 00:17:34.009
- Are you okay?
- Somehow.

00:17:34.788 --> 00:17:36.483
- Hubb, take Cheza.
- Sure.

00:18:02.315 --> 00:18:03.077
Cher...

00:18:03.716 --> 00:18:04.683
Cher!

00:18:05.585 --> 00:18:06.677
Cher!

00:18:08.354 --> 00:18:09.878
Cher...

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:16.952
I can hear you,
Hubb...

00:18:17.831 --> 00:18:20.925
You've turned into
a real man...

00:18:21.935 --> 00:18:25.894
Yeah. 'Cause I have
to look out for you.

00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:30.004
We can start over
from scratch.

00:18:33.279 --> 00:18:36.737
Let's have...
Let's have kids.

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:42.745
We'll bake bread, and...

00:18:44.190 --> 00:18:46.488
I know, let's get
a little bird, too...

00:18:48.094 --> 00:18:50.062
It'll all work out
this time.

00:18:50.630 --> 00:18:52.097
Everything will
work out.

00:18:56.436 --> 00:18:57.528
Cher...?

00:18:58.171 --> 00:18:59.263
Cher?

00:19:01.808 --> 00:19:03.537
Cher...

00:19:07.547 --> 00:19:09.777
CHER!

00:19:11.384 --> 00:19:12.783
CHER!

00:19:13.386 --> 00:19:14.944
CHER!

00:19:16.489 --> 00:19:17.513
Cher...!

00:19:19.526 --> 00:19:21.517
Cher...

00:21:22.215 --> 00:21:24.513
You're going to keep
moving on, right?

00:21:24.851 --> 00:21:25.783
Yeah.

00:21:26.119 --> 00:21:27.518
I'll escort you.

00:21:30.857 --> 00:21:34.020
I don't know how far
I'll be able to go,

00:21:35.895 --> 00:21:39.831
but I'll make sure you get to where
you're going, no matter what.

00:21:42.068 --> 00:21:45.037
Where the Soul Goes

00:23:05.084 --> 00:23:06.085
Next Time
<i> </i>
<i> </i>
<i> </i>

00:23:06.085 --> 00:23:07.086
Next Time
<i> </i>
Partings are
always sudden.

00:23:07.086 --> 00:23:07.780
Partings are
always sudden.

00:23:08.421 --> 00:23:11.324
It doesn't matter if you're sitting around shivering,
or sleeping, or in the middle of eating,

00:23:11.324 --> 00:23:13.758
they always sneak up on you
when you least expect it.

00:23:14.394 --> 00:23:17.096
That reminds me, I'm hungry...
When was the last time we ate?

00:23:17.096 --> 00:23:18.164
Gunshot of Remorse
